These historical results predate the full-payload SHA256D key correction
in the preceding commit. Its added per-request hashing is not measured
here; these tables do not establish performance of the corrected tree.
Raw TCP does not use the independent-frame cache.

Node CPU min-max ranges do not overlap in any cell. Wall time is noisy
under this load: the 32 MB WebSocket cells (B/A 0.75-0.85) have
overlapping ranges, and peers decoding 32 MB blocks compete with the
node and the other agents for CPUs. Wire bytes are unchanged.

How to reproduce: build the previous commit and this one (Release), then

    python3 contrib/bench/ws-block-frames/serve_ab.py \
        --base <previous-build> --patched <this-build> --output <dir> \
        --transport tcp --sizes 1,8,32 --peers 8,32,64 --rounds 5
    (and again with --transport ws)

Not tested: Linux and other platforms, sanitizers, the full functional
suite, pruned nodes serving recent blocks under load, mainnet blocks.

Tier: eCash

